<!--
  Canonical pages only.

  `/faq`, `/cookies`, `/seller-agreement` and `/prohibited-items` are deliberately
  absent. Each renders another page's row (/faq is the About content, /cookies is
  Privacy, /seller-agreement and /prohibited-items are Terms) and each declares
  that page's URL as its canonical, so see LEGAL_PAGES in src/lib/pageSeo.ts.
  Submitting a URL while telling Google its canonical is a different URL is a
  contradictory signal: the alias spends crawl budget and Search Console reports
  "Duplicate, submitted URL not selected as canonical". Those four routes stay
  linked, prerendered and reachable, they are just not submitted.

  Department (/categories/<slug>) and collection (/collections/<slug>) URLs come
  from database rows, so a static file cannot list them; they are discovered
  through /categories and each prerendered page declares its own canonical.
-->
